# <imperative verb> <what>[: <elaboration>][; <second concern>]
# Aim for <=72 chars. Sentence case, no trailing period, no type: prefix.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Why this change. Not what the diff already says.
#
# If this is a fix or a reversal: what was wrong before, and why the new
# version is right. The reader six months from now is deciding whether it
# is safe to change it back.
#
# Reference stable identifiers so the history stays greppable:
#   A4-12  BF-11  J10  RULE-4  §9.6
#
# If you seriously considered another approach, say why it lost. A commit
# that records the rejected alternative prevents someone re-taking it.
#
# Wrap at 72-80 columns. Plain ASCII in the body.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Before committing:
#   [ ] TODOS.md ticked, or task added/split/[-] with a reason
#   [ ] CHANGELOG.md if observable behaviour, a format, or a default changed
#   [ ] DEVLOG.md if a decision was reversed or an assumption overturned
#   [ ] PLAN.md corrected in THIS change if the implementation contradicts it
#
# Never amend or reset a pushed commit. Never --no-verify.
